<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Fiji</h1><p class="st-meta">1970 CE – present · capital Suva</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Pacific archipelago republic, independent from Britain in 1970, with military coups in 1987 and 2006 and a return to elections in 2014.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-fiji">Colony of Fiji</a> was established by the British in 1874. A cabinet system began in 1967 with Ratu Kamisese Mara as the first Chief Minister, after constitutional conferences in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1965 and 1970. Fiji became independent at midnight on 9 October 1970 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> of Fiji, and the flag was raised on 10 October.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Two military coups in 1987 followed a perception that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-fijians">Indo-Fijians</a> dominated the government; the monarchy ended and Fiji became a republic. A 1990 constitution institutionalised ethnic Fijian dominance, and a new constitution was written in 1997. Mahendra Chaudhry became the first Indo-Fijian prime minister that year and was toppled in a coup led by George Speight in 2000. Commodore Frank Bainimarama seized power in 2006, and in 2009 the president abrogated the constitution. Heavy Indo-Fijian emigration made Melanesians the majority.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>An election on 17 September 2014 returned Bainimarama's FijiFirst party with 59.2% of the vote, and international observers deemed it credible. The Commonwealth suspension was lifted in September 2014. Ratu Wiliame Katonivere was elected president in October 2021. Sitiveni Rabuka became prime minister on 24 December 2022 after the general election.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/fiji.jpg" alt="Fiji" width="330" height="165"><figcaption>Image: Tessa Mackenzie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Fiji.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1970 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Suva</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kamisese Mara, Sitiveni Rabuka, Mahendra Chaudhry, Laisenia Qarase, Frank Bainimarama</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christian (mainly Methodist), Hindu, Muslim</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Fijian, Fiji Hindi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/fiji">Fiji</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Fiji</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1998&amp;focus=fiji" aria-label="Fiji on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: where Fiji lay"><image href="/maps/globes/g180s30.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4873 3993L4905 3955"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4905 3955h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4873 3993h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4873 3993h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Suva. <a href="/atlas?year=1998&amp;focus=fiji">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
